.TH VDR-SUITE-FIRST-ADMIN-BOOTSTRAP 8 "September 2026" "VDR-Suite" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
vdr-suite-first-admin-bootstrap \- issue short-lived first-admin setup material
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdr-suite-first-admin-bootstrap
.RI [ --database " PATH" ]
.RI [ --ttl-seconds " 300..3600" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vdr-suite-first-admin-bootstrap
is a local root-only administration command for an unclaimed VDR-Suite server.
It creates cryptographically random, short-lived first-admin bootstrap material
in the existing Suite security database.
.PP
The raw setup secret is printed once to standard output. Only a one-way verifier,
the bootstrap identifier, expiry and lifecycle metadata are persisted.
The setup secret is not a normal account password, browser session or reusable
API credential.
.PP
The command refuses issuance after the server is already claimed and while an
effective unconsumed bootstrap issuance exists.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --database " PATH"
Use the specified Suite database instead of
.IR /var/lib/vdr-suite/vdr-suite.db .
.TP
.BI --ttl-seconds " SECONDS"
Set bootstrap lifetime. The accepted range is 300 through 3600 seconds.
The default is 900 seconds.
.SH OUTPUT
On success, the command prints exactly one bootstrap identifier, setup secret
and expiry timestamp:
.PP
.nf
bootstrap_id=...
setup_secret=...
expires_at=...
.fi
.PP
Treat the setup secret as transient security material. It is intended only for
the later first-admin claim flow and cannot be recovered from the database.
.SH SECURITY
The command must be run as root. Remote anonymous callers cannot invoke this
local command through the VDR-Suite HTTP API. No plaintext bootstrap secret is
written to package configuration or persistent Suite state.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/vdr-suite/vdr-suite.db
Default Suite security database.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vdr-suite-daemon (8)
